 "notes": "ALPS light-shining-through-wall experiment (DESY, HERA dipole). Curve is the 95% C.L. pseudoscalar ALP limit g- from Fig. 4 (left panel), extracted from the vector fill regions of pics/alpminus.pdf in the e-print. Reported curve is the boundary of the union of the 'ALPS' (vacuum runs) and 'ALPS(gas)' (0.18 mbar Ar) excluded regions, i.e. the paper's total excluded region; the gas runs fill the coherence gaps of the vacuum data. Flat limit ~6.5e-8 GeV^-1 below ~5e-4 eV; figure range 1e-4 to ~3.6e-3 eV (limit continues flat to lower masses). Pseudoscalar coupling defined via L = -(g-/4) F Fdual phi, Eq. (1), identical to the canonical convention, so no conversion applied. Points at g~2e-6 near high-mass oscillation peaks are capped by the figure's top edge. Scalar ALP (g+, Fig. 4 right), hidden photon (Fig. 5) and minicharged particle (Fig. 6) limits also reported but pseudoscalar ALP limit taken as the main axion-photon result. Laboratory bound: no dark-matter density assumption.",
